  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "escrow-explained",
      "title": "Understanding your escrow account",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Your monthly payment includes $1,412.50 for escrow. We hold these funds in an escrow account and use them to pay your property taxes, homeowners insurance and flood insurance on your behalf when they come due.",
        "Once a year we complete an escrow analysis to compare what we expect to pay over the next 12 months with what we collect. If the account is projected to have a surplus of $50 or more, we refund it to you. If it is projected to have a shortage, you can pay the shortage in one lump sum or spread it over the next 12 payments.",
        "Your most recent analysis (January 2026) found a surplus of $642.18, which was refunded by check on February 9, 2026. Your monthly escrow amount increased from $1,356.25 to $1,412.50 because your property tax installments increased by 4.8% and your homeowners insurance premium increased by 4.7%."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "late-fee",
      "title": "Late fee notice",
      "paragraphs": [
        "If we do not receive your full payment by November 16, 2026, we will charge a late fee of $399.28. That is 4% of the principal and interest portion of your payment, as allowed by your note.",
        "Payments made online before 8:00 p.m. Eastern time on a business day are credited the same day. Payments that are not enough to cover a full monthly payment are held in a suspense account and are not applied to your loan until the remaining funds are received."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assistance",
      "title": "If you are having trouble making payments",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Call Borrower Assistance at 1-800-555-0142 (synthetic number), Monday to Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. Eastern time. You may be eligible for a repayment plan, forbearance or a loan modification. Housing counselors approved by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development can also help at no cost."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "important",
      "title": "Important messages",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Partial payments: any partial payment we receive will not be applied to your mortgage but will be held in a separate suspense account. Once there are enough funds in suspense to cover a full monthly payment, we will apply them to your loan.",
        "Credit reporting: we may report information about your account to credit bureaus. Late payments, missed payments or other defaults on your account may be reflected in your credit report.",
        "This is a synthetic statement produced for the Interface Foundry demo. Harborline Home Loans is fictional; no real customer, account or property data is shown."
      ]
    }
  ]
